// MathGeometryDrills are the math and geometry foundations: peeling digits with
// % 10 and // 10 (reverse an integer), Euclid's gcd and the lcm that follows from
// it, the square-root bound for primality, the sieve of Eratosthenes (Count
// Primes), fast exponentiation with a modulus, transposing a matrix and walking
// it by diagonals, and the cross-product orientation test with exact integer
// arithmetic. They build up to Happy Number, Pow(x, n), Rotate Image, Spiral
// Matrix and the geometry-flavoured ladder problems without repeating them.
// Where speed matters (trial division against the square-root bound, a sieve
// against a prime test per number, a linear loop against repeated squaring) the
// tests include an input that only the intended algorithm finishes on in time.
// Every explanation says why the identity holds. They follow docs/pedagogy.md
// like any problem.
